  "name": "INTERLEUKIN 6(IL6) (FC)",
  "code": "1773",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Comments- </strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">IL-6 is a sensitive parameter and results change with temp and time from collection of sample. Accuracy of</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">results depends on integrity of sample (cold chain maintenance, timing of collection and transport of sample). Repeat with&nbsp;fresh sample is recommended in case high value is not correlating with clinical condition.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Interpretation :- </strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">1. Interleukin-6(IL-6) is a pleiotropic cytokine with a wide range of functions.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">2. IL-6 production is rapidly induced in the course of acute inflammatory reactions associated with injury trauma ,stress, </span><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">infection, brain death, neoplasia and other situations.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">3. IL-6 concentration in trauma patients may predict later complications from additional surgical stress or indicate missed </span><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">injuries or complications.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">4. Sequential measurements of IL-6 in serum or plasma of patients admitted to the ICU showed it to be useful in evaluating</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">the severity of SIRS (Systemic inflammatory response syndrome), sepsis and septic shock and to predict the outcome of </span><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">these patients.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">5. IL-6 is also useful as an early alarm marker for the detection of neonatal sepsis.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">6. IL-6 also plays a role in chronic inflammation eg. Rheumatoid arthritis(RA)</span></p>",
